<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (The Alumni Cell of the Indian Institute of Information Technology \(IIIT\) Pune launched the first-ever edition of "Alumni Speaks" on September 29th, 2026. The session began at 16:30 in the Auditorium. It was a completely student-led initiative, created to build a stronger and more connected student community through meaningful interaction between seniors, juniors and alumni.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (The inaugural speaker was Mr. Darshan Lokhande, a proud IIIT Pune alumnus and Software Engineer at Google. At Google, he works on Web Indexing and Information Retrieval systems that operate at massive scale. With nearly four years of experience across Google and Nutanix, he has contributed to and improved large-scale backend systems. A Computer Science graduate of IIIT Pune, he is also a three-time International Collegiate Programming Contest \(ICPC\) Regionalist, which reflects his strong expertise in algorithms and problem-solving.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (Mr. Lokhande shared insights from his journey, his career experiences, industry expectations, the opportunities ahead and the transition from college to the professional world. It was far more than a series of stories. Students brought their questions and received practical, honest guidance from a senior who has successfully made the journey from IIIT Pune to Google. The conversation covered placements, career opportunities and everything students wished to ask openly.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (The energy in the room showed how much students value such conversations. The Alumni Cell is thrilled by the response and is determined to make "Alumni Speaks" a regular feature of campus life. It plans to host many more editions and to bring more alumni from diverse fields back to campus, so that every student has a senior to learn from.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
