226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (On October 1st, 2026, as part of the Swachhata Hi Seva 2026 campaign, IIIT Pune organised a SafaiMitra Suraksha Evam Samman Shivir to recognise and engage with the sanitation workers contributing to the cleanliness and hygiene of the campus. The initiative highlighted the importance of waste segregation, responsible waste management, clean water, and composting as key practices for a sustainable campus. It also emphasised the importance of dignity, safety, and respect for sanitation workers and recognised their contribution to the Institute community.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (The programme supported SDG 3, Good Health and Well Being, SDG 6, Clean Water and Sanitation, SDG 11, Sustainable Cities and Communities, SDG 12, Responsible Consumption and Production, and SDG 13, Climate Action through its focus on hygiene, sanitation, resource conservation, responsible waste management, and environmental sustainability.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [13]
>>
